
- The quiescent power consumption of the LDO should be no larger than 1000 μW.
- The DC loop gain of the LDO should be at least 45 dB.
- The loop gain-bandwidth product (GBW) should be at least 300000 Hz.
- The phase margin should be at least 50 degrees.
- The power supply rejection ratio (PSRR) at DC should be at least 30 dB.
- The line regulation (LNR) should be no larger than 0.1 V/V per volt of supply change.
- The load regulation (LR) should be no larger than 1 per ampere of load change.
- The output voltage offset (vos) at maximum load should be no larger than 0.08 V.
- The transient undershoot under a 10 μA to 10 mA load step should be no larger than 0.5 V.
- The transient overshoot under a 10 mA to 10 μA load step should be no larger than 0.5 V.
